Here's what the investigation found and what was changed:

---

## Investigation results

There are **two** `WMQConstants` classes and one `MQConstants` class in the IBM MQ installation:

| Class | Package | JAR | Has `WMQ_CCDTURL` / `WMQ_QUEUE_MANAGER`? |
|-------|---------|-----|------------------------------------------|
| `WMQConstants` | `com.ibm.msg.client.jakarta.wmq` | `com.ibm.mq.jakarta.client.jar` ✅ | **Yes** — `"XMSC_WMQ_CCDTURL"` / `"XMSC_WMQ_QUEUE_MANAGER"` |
| `MQConstants` | `com.ibm.mq.constants` | `com.ibm.mq.jakarta.client.jar` ❌ | **No** — these constants are absent |
| `WMQConstants` | `com.ibm.msg.client.wmq` | `com.ibm.mq.allclient.jar` ❌ | Yes (same values) — but wrong JAR for jakarta projects |

**`MQConstants` does not contain the needed constants** — it only implements the MQI PCF/CMQC/CMQXC interface hierarchy. `WMQ_CCDTURL` and `WMQ_QUEUE_MANAGER` belong exclusively to `WMQConstants`.

## Changes made

- **[`ConsumerWorker.java`](srcj/com/example/mqconsumer/ConsumerWorker.java:4)** — import changed from `com.ibm.msg.client.wmq.WMQConstants` → `com.ibm.msg.client.jakarta.wmq.WMQConstants`
- **[`ProducerWorker.java`](srcj/com/example/mqproducer/ProducerWorker.java:4)** — same import fix
- **[`BUILDING.md`](BUILDING.md)** — removed `com.ibm.mq.allclient.jar` from all classpath commands; `jakarta\*` wildcard alone is sufficient
- **[`jms-consumer-plan.md`](jms-consumer-plan.md)** — Sub-Task 4 Relevant Context updated with the correct import, verified constant values, and explicit warnings against `MQConstants` and `allclient.jar`
- **[`jms-producer-plan.md`](jms-producer-plan.md)** — Sub-Task 5 Relevant Context updated identically
- **[`README.md`](README.md)** — new "WMQConstants — classpath investigation findings" section with the comparison table

